{title: He Rode Upon the Cherub}
{subtitle: Psalm 18}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 143}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] | [A] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]In my distress I [C]called upon the [Dm]Lord
To [Bb]my God I [C]cried for [Dm]help
From his [Bb]temple he [C]heard my [Dm]voice
My cry came be[Bb]fore him, into his [A]ears
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Then the earth reeled and rocked
The foundations of the [C]mountains trem[Dm]bled
Smoke went up from his nostrils
De[Bb]vouring fire from his [C]mouth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Dm]rode upon [F]a [C]cherub and [Dm]flew
He came [Bb]swiftly on the [F]wings of the [C]wind
He reached from [Dm]on high, [F]he took [C]me
He drew me [Bb]out of [A]many wa[Dm]ters [Bb][C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]The Lord thundered in the heavens
[C]The Most High uttered his [Dm]voice
He [Bb]sent out his arrows and [C]scattered them
[Bb]Lightnings and [C]routed [Dm][Bb][C]them
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] | ×5

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Dm]rode upon [F]a [C]cherub and [Dm]flew
He came [Bb]swiftly on the [F]wings of the [C]wind
He reached from [Dm]on high, [F]he took [C]me
He drew me [Bb]out of [C]many waters [Dm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The Lord is my [F]rock, my [C]fortress and [Dm]my deliv[Bb]er[F]er
{end_of_verse}

